## Freeze backend cards in view mode

Context: Domain → Information backend cards used hidden radio inputs. The
generic read-only CSS blocked pointer events on those inputs, but their labels
could still activate them and keyboard navigation could still change the
selected backend. Viewers and edit-locked users must not be able to alter this
domain setting.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/domain/js/domain-information.js
   Natively disables backend card radios for read-only versions, viewer roles,
   and edit locks; resynchronizes after lifecycle evaluation and whenever body
   permission classes change.
2. tests/units/front/test_no_backend_ui.py
   Added regression contracts covering all three view-only states and
   mid-session permission changes.

Modified files:
- src/front/static/domain/js/domain-information.js
- tests/units/front/test_no_backend_ui.py
- changelogs/v0.8.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-08-31.log

Tests: uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" → 5739 passed, 305 skipped, 6 deselected, 1 xfailed, 23 warnings in 51.73s.

Browser verification: `.role-viewer`, `.read-only-version`, and
`.read-only-locked` all natively disabled the four backend radios; pointer and
keyboard selection remained frozen, while removing the view-only state restored
interaction.

## Match Domain Information tab surface

Context: Domain → Information used a standalone bordered tab-content surface,
while the requested Ontology → Data Quality reference places its tab rail and
content inside one card. The separate surfaces produced different visible
borders, radii, spacing, and rail edges despite sharing the same tab component.

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_information.html
   Rebuilt the tab container with the Data Quality `card h-100` /
   `card-body p-0` structure, `nav-fill` rail, and `tab-content p-3` body.
2. tests/units/front/test_no_backend_ui.py
   Added regression contracts for the Data Quality tab-header classes and
   single-card surface structure.

Modified files:
- src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_information.html
- tests/units/front/test_no_backend_ui.py
- changelogs/v0.8.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-08-31.log

Tests: uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" → 5740 passed, 305 skipped, 6 deselected, 1 xfailed, 23 warnings in 52.04s.

Browser verification: Domain Information matched the Data Quality card border,
radius, background, content padding, and flush rail geometry; tab switching,
responsive overflow, backend cards, and read-only locking remained functional.

## Standardize card-integrated page tabs

Context: Ontology → Generate still used a standalone `ob-tab-content` surface
under the tab rail, while Domain → Information and Ontology → Data Quality
share one outer card. The Cursor rule treated all tab bodies as independent
surfaces, so new pages kept drifting away from the Data Quality reference.

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_wizard.html
   Wrapped the Generate tabs in the Data Quality `card h-100` /
   `card-body p-0 ob-tabs-wrap` structure with a `nav-fill` rail and
   `tab-content p-3` body.
2. .cursor/11-frontend-design.mdc
   Documented card-integrated page tabs as the default page-level pattern
   and kept `ob-tab-content` for genuinely independent surfaces.
3. .claude/skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md
   Added a thin Claude skill that points to `.cursor/11` and sequences
   contract tests plus browser verification.
4. CLAUDE.md
   Registered the `frontend-design` skill in the Claude-only skill table.
5. tests/units/front/test_clarity_design_contract.py
   Added contracts for Generate markup, the Cursor rule skeleton, and the
   Claude skill pointer.
6. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-31-card-integrated-tabs-design.md
   Recorded the approved design for the card-integrated tab pattern.
7. docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-31-card-integrated-tabs.md
   Recorded the test-first implementation plan.

